    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d377">

                <pb facs="0421" n="345" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg345"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.51/470</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Secretary of the Navy
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 26, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your letter of January 21, 1916, with which you were good enough to
                    enclose a copy of the report of the Commander of the Cruiser Squadron, Atlantic
                    Fleet, at Port au Prince, Haiti, on the system adopted for paying employees of
                    the Haitian Government.</p>
                <p>I have read this report with interest and desire to commend the efficient
                    disposition that Admiral Caperton has made of the means at his disposal to carry
                    out the purpose of this Government to safeguard as far as possible the interests
                    of all concerned.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
